AB  - This work is motivated by a common urban renewal process called Reconstruct and Divide. It involves the demolition of old buildings and the construction of new ones. Original homeowners are compensated with upgraded apartments, while surplus units are sold for profit, so theoretically it is a win-win project for all parties involved. However, many Reconstruct and Divide projects are withheld or delayed due to disagreements over the assignment of new apartments, claiming they are not fair. The goal of this research is to develop algorithms for envy-free assignment of the new apartments, possibly using monetary payments to reduce envy.
