AB  - We study an online fair division problem where a fixed, but unknown number of goods arrive sequentially and must be allocated immediately and irrevocably to a given set of agents. The objective is to ensure (approximate) envy-freeness up to any good (EFX), that is, after the allocation, no agent should prefer another agent's bundle once any single good is removed from it. Unfortunately, we show that approximate EFX is impossible to guarantee, even under restrictive valuation assumptions.
