AB  - The interpretation of proportionality in multiwinner voting differs significantly from that in apportionment. We aim to bridge them by introducing the concept of allocation proportionality: a voting rule is allocation proportional if each party's share of elected candidates equals that party's aggregate score. We introduce a new measure of allocation proportionality degree, and use it to experimentally evaluate a number of common OWA--based voting rules.
